
Scenario: generateMainMenuHTMLIntegrationTest | Verifies that generating the main menu HTML includes the document structure, menu title and heading, navigation links, audit link, and logout link.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Main menu" and the five supplied menu options
THEN the generated HTML contains the DOCTYPE declaration, Main Menu title and heading, links for browsing briefs, agents, facilities, and missions, the audit link, and the logout link.

Scenario: generateBrowsePageHTMLIntegrationTest | Verifies that generating the browse page HTML includes record content, a read form, and navigation back to the main menu.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Browse: missions" and mission details
THEN the generated HTML contains the DOCTYPE declaration, Browse missions title and heading, mission ID and title, a form targeting `/read` with the missions type, and a Back to Main Menu link targeting `/`.
